  Why: 'The St Peters key-scene boards'' cliffs (terrain pass 9 west and east ledges, the south arm, the lighthouse point): the lit beds a lighter, more orange red-brown than ours (board rock modes about #b06848 to #b87050 against our #a6583b base), a darker brown cap where the till sits under the turf, and grey-green interbeds where our siltstone is. Read off the boards by eye and by their rock pixel counts (seat/v83/cliffs-mix/board-colours.txt) and cut into tiers and bands by the px kit''s own procedure, so the cold shadows and warm lights lean exactly as the shipped palette''s do.'
